# Swiss Post crypto-primitives 1.6.0, section 10.5, algorithm 10.10:
# two ciphertexts under different keys carry the same plaintext.
# phi(r, r') = (g^r, g^r', h^r / h'^r'), so the third base for r' is
# the inverse of the second public key.
secrets r r_
claims  r r_
eq  c0       g  1
eq  c0_      1  g
eq  c1/c1_   h  inv_h_

# An instance: one distinct generator per base name, so the
# environment is faithful and the verdict above transfers to it.
# The exponents are ours and carry no meaning; every element of a
# prime-order group is a generator power, so this is simply a way
# to write distinct elements down.
point g       2
point h       3
point inv_h_  5
